      "hints": [
        "Differentiate $y = 8x^{1/2} - 2x$ to get $\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}} - 2$.",
        "Set $\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}} - 2 = 0 \\implies x = 4$, giving point $(4, 8)$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Differentiate the curve equation with respect to $x$:\n$$\\frac{dy}{dx} = 8\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)x^{-\\frac{1}{2}} - 2 = \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}} - 2$$",
        "Set $\\frac{dy}{dx} = 0$ to find the stationary point:\n$$\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}} - 2 = 0 \\implies \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}} = 2 \\implies \\sqrt{x} = 2 \\implies x = 4$$",
        "Calculate the corresponding $y$-coordinate:\n$$y = 8\\sqrt{4} - 2(4) = 8(2) - 8 = 8$$\n$$\\text{Stationary point: } (4, 8)$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
        "ai_rubric": {
          "Stationary Point": "Differentiates to $\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}} - 2$ (B1). Solves for $x = 4$ (B1) and $y = 8$ (B1)."
        },
        "criteria_source": "mark_scheme_structured"
      }
