      "hints": [
        "Set $8\\sqrt{x} - 2x = 6 \\implies x - 4\\sqrt{x} + 3 = 0$.",
        "Factorise $(\\sqrt{x} - 1)(\\sqrt{x} - 3) = 0 \\implies x = 1, 9$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Set the curve equation equal to $y = 6$:\n$$8\\sqrt{x} - 2x = 6 \\implies 2x - 8\\sqrt{x} + 6 = 0 \\implies x - 4\\sqrt{x} + 3 = 0$$",
        "Substitute $u = \\sqrt{x}$ to form a quadratic in $u$:\n$$u^2 - 4u + 3 = 0 \\implies (u - 1)(u - 3) = 0$$\n$$u = 1 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad u = 3$$",
        "Square each root to find $x$:\n$$\\sqrt{x} = 1 \\implies x = 1$$\n$$\\sqrt{x} = 3 \\implies x = 9$$\n$$(\\text{Values of } x: \\quad x = 1, \\quad 9)$$"
      ],
